==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{m|roa-opt|bairro}}, {{m|roa-opt|barrio}}, from {{etyl|ar|pt}} {{m|ar||tr=barrī}}, referring to the outer, surrounding or less civilized or urbanized parts of a city. Compare Spanish ''[[barrio]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/ˈbaj.ʁu/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|bair|ro|lang=pt}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|m}}

# {{l|en|neighborhood}}, {{l|en|area}} {{gloss|of a city}}

